<title>EGYPT: Egypt port confiscates 52,500 T French wheat cargo.</title>
<headline>Egypt port confiscates 52,500 T French wheat cargo.</headline>
<dateline>PORT SAID, Egypt 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's Port Said authorities said on Thursday they had confiscated an Algerian cargo ship on suspicion that its cargo of French wheat also contained poppy pods.</p>
<p>They said the ship, El Hadjar, was carrying 52,500 tonnes of French wheat bought by the state's General Authority for Supply Commodities from Dunkirk to Egypt.</p>
<p>Port officials confiscated the ship after tests showed traces of poppy seeds. The drug opium is extracted from poppies.</p>
<p>El-Hadjar will remain in the port until the cargo is further analysed, the port said.</p>
</text>
